      "content": "Fragmentation means that standardized protocols for inventory allocation and emergency rerouting will be replaced by local, potentially suboptimal decisions. During a major disruption, a single node failure won't halt the entire network, but localized blackouts could lead to cascading shortages in specific geographic regions due to poor inter-node communication. Projecting failure rates for life-critical medication is complex, but without centralized oversight, we project a 15-25% increase in delivery delays during a Tier-1 regional event compared to the current centralized model.",
