    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The 25% figure represents a high-end projection based on current infrastructure maturity and assumes no immediate investment in advanced inter-node communication protocols. These failures are not strictly unavoidable, but they are the baseline risk without proactive measures. To mitigate this, we could implement a lightweight, supervisory \"meta-orchestration\" layer that oversees regional nodes without controlling their daily operations. This hybrid approach retains localization benefits while providing a safety net for catastrophic cross-regional failures.",
      "source": "target",
